<Project>

  <!--
    THE observability switch: the one place the mode of the kernel's observability rules is decided.

      report   (the committed default)  the rules are reported and counted, and nothing fails: the self-analysis
                                         runs the SK analyzers and CA2200 at warning (listed in WarningsNotAsErrors),
                                         and the platform-wide assertions print a per-domain table.
      enforce                           the same analyzers run at error and the assertions throw one aggregated
                                         exception.

    Flipping to failing is the single edit of the value below: change report to enforce.

    Two consumers read this property, so they cannot disagree:
      - SharedKernel.SelfAnalysis.props picks kernel-report.globalconfig or kernel-enforce.globalconfig and the
        WarningsNotAsErrors list from it, for every kernel project under src/.
      - SharedKernel.ArchitectureTests.Tests imports this file and stamps the value into its assembly as
        AssemblyMetadata("SharedKernelObservabilityMode", ...), which ObservabilityEnforcement.Configured reads.
    A command-line -p:SharedKernelObservabilityMode=... wins over this file for a local experiment (MSBuild global
    properties outrank file properties); the environment variable SHAREDKERNEL_OBSERVABILITY_MODE does the same for
    the assertions.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SharedKernelObservabilityMode>report</SharedKernelObservabilityMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
